Unwind the link stack when break or next appears in a complex assignment's value.

cmpComplexAssign() pushes an INCLNKSTK marker before compiling the value.
The non-tail-call context lets a break or next compile as a direct GOTO,
which skips DECLNKSTK. The loop exit then reads the leftover link stack
marker as a loop context and can crash. Compile the value in an argument
context so control flow goes through the existing unwind path.

A smaller reproducer is:
    Rscript --vanilla -e 'library(compiler); cmpfun(function() 1 - repeat x[1] <- break)()'

The upstream PR also adds a regression test
(src/library/compiler/tests/loop.R), not carried here.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 5106865747591168.
R Bugzilla: https://bugs.r-project.org/show_bug.cgi?id=19252

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #409, filed 2026-10-26.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

--- a/src/library/compiler/R/cmp.R
+++ b/src/library/compiler/R/cmp.R
@@ -1727,7 +1727,8 @@ cmpComplexAssign <- function(symbol, lhs, value, superAssign, cb, cntxt) {
         endOP <- ENDASSIGN.OP
     }
     if (! cntxt$toplevel) cb$putcode(INCLNKSTK.OP)
-    ncntxt <- make.nonTailCallContext(cntxt)
+    ## A break or next in value must unwind the link stack marker above.
+    ncntxt <- make.argContext(cntxt)
     cmp(value, cb, ncntxt)
     csi <- cb$putconst(symbol)
     cb$putcode(startOP, csi)
